        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Book of the Dead</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1700 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Written by many priests over about 1,000 years, drawing on the older <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-texts">Pyramid Texts</a> and Coffin Texts; each copy made to order by scribes and artists in funerary workshops</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">A loose collection of some 192 known spells in hieroglyphic or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hieratic">hieratic</a> script, in black and red ink on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a> scrolls from about 1 m to 40 m long, often illustrated with vignettes</span></div>
